================================================================================================
v116  SYMPLECTIC PRE-FLIGHT:  one GF(2) check, two obstructions
================================================================================================
  For a twirl-multiplexed degree-1 Walsh decode, the term set alone decides
  whether the decode is confounded and whether time reversal is free.
  TIER C: operator structure, no state evolution. R1-sanctioned.

================================================================================================
THE FAMILIES
================================================================================================
  crosstalk N=3          N=3  M=9   rank(V)=5   2N=6
     dependencies forced by M > rank : True
     degree-2 aliasing triples       : 6   e.g. ZZI + XXI = YYI
     odd null subsets (block Q)      : 4
     time-reversing twirl Q          : NO
     -> kernel needs the cross-Pauli readout; no cheap fix

  crosstalk N=4          N=4  M=13  rank(V)=7   2N=8
