================================================================================================
READING IT
================================================================================================
  THE RULE. If any ODD-size subset of terms has symplectic vectors summing
  to zero, then the flip parity over that subset is fixed at even for every
  twirl - so all-minus is unreachable, no Q reverses time, and the same null
  combination confounds a degree-2 product with a degree-1 effect.

  crosstalk fails on both counts at every N, and for one reason:
     v(ZZ) + v(XX) + v(YY) = 0   on every bond
  The XX/YY/ZZ triple is the whole story - it caps the weak ZZ coefficients
  (v106) and blocks the free kernel fix (v115) simultaneously.

  USE IT AS A PRE-FLIGHT. Before building a twirl-multiplexed estimator for
  a new term set:
     odd_nulls empty  -> decode is clean at degree 2 AND time reversal is
                         free, so the band-limited kernel drops straight in
     odd_nulls found  -> expect a weak-coefficient ceiling, and budget for
                         the cross-Pauli restructure rather than a patch

  This session lost two builds to questions answered here in milliseconds.

  Scope: alias search is over PAIRS and odd nulls up to size 4. Larger even
  dependencies exist whenever M > rank and are not enumerated - they affect
  higher-degree confounding, not the two obstructions above.
